# Default deny. The kit is public and deliberately project-agnostic, while this
# working tree has held audit, debate, sweep and repair artifacts describing
# private consuming repositories, including unremediated security findings. Those
# must never be published here, and anything similar that lands here later is
# private by default rather than by someone remembering to exclude it.
#
# This file previously listed the artifacts to exclude, which fails open: any new
# artifact whose name matched no pattern became publishable, and a `git add -A` did
# once commit nine private files. It now ignores everything and re-admits only what
# the kit actually publishes, so a new file is private unless someone deliberately
# adds it below.
#
# Published: the shared payload under _strata/, README, LICENSE,
# and the two git control files. Everything else — reports, plans, ledgers, fixtures,
# tooling, scratch — stays local.

*

!.gitattributes
!.gitignore
!LICENSE
!AGENTS.md
!CLAUDE.md
!README.md

!_strata/
!_strata/**
